WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.920
A familiar staff, a wizard's past mistakes,
and a minotaur in the Big Apple?

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.962
These are the little things you may have missed
in the new trailer for "Shazam: Fury of the Gods."

00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:15.651
We know that Shazam's back to save the day
in "Fury of the Gods," but who exactly is

00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:17.570
the big bad of the sequel?

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.750
Just going by the cast list, it's easy to
assume that Helen Mirren's Hespera is the

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.060
film's main villain.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:28.199
Still, looking at the trailer, Hespera's role
kind of seems closer to a DCU equivalent to

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:32.651
the MCU's Odin— a powerful figure who's
done a bunch of awful stuff in the past, but

00:00:32.651 --> 00:00:38.110
generally takes a more advisory role to their
younger proteges by the time the movie has started.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.629
"You are very menacing."

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:44.720
Lucy Liu's Kalypso, on the other hand, is
another thing entirely.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.329
She's the one who makes the best ominous poses,
and demolishes sports stadiums with her monstrous

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:50.670
green thumb.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.790
And that's not even to mention the fact that
she's the one with the cool, dark costume.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:57.449
Oh, and she's riding an actual dragon.

00:00:57.449 --> 00:01:01.269
We don't know yet whether Kalypso is going
to be the secret power behind the throne or

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:06.520
just a very imposing lackey to Mirren's Hespera,
but either way, it's great to see Lucy Liu

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.770
back on the big screen in a big way.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.310
One of the most eye-catching visual elements
of the "Shazam!

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:16.600
Fury of the Gods" trailers comes in the form
of a magical staff brimming with blue energy.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.100
At different points in the trailer, viewers
can see both the villains and the hero all

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.939
using the staff during various big blowout
battles.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:27.790
However, it seems that none of these characters
are actually the true owner of the weapon.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:31.990
By all accounts, the staff actually belongs
to The Wizard Shazam himself.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.380
Viewers of the original "Shazam!"

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.630
may recall that The Wizard uses what is presumably
the exact same staff to grant Billy his powers.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.570
And speaking of Billy's powers, it's not looking
too good for the Big Red Cheese.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:46.180
"The Daughters of Atlas are coming to hunt
us."

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.020
Based on the newest trailer, it seems like
those fearsome daughters have the perfect

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.320
weapon to do so.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.540
In one moment in the trailer, Mary Marvel
is forcibly transformed back into her mortal

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.759
form by the staff, losing the one thing that
gives her a fighting chance against the bad guys.

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:04.759
While the idea of superheroes losing their
powers isn't necessarily novel, it'll be interesting

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:07.850
to see how the Shazam family takes on this
adversity.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.380
Both trailers show that everyone is having
a great time with their new abilities, so

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.959
losing the powers they've come to rely on
might be a big blow to the Marvel family.

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:19.019
But it's not all doom and gloom for Shazam
fans.

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:23.190
Most excitingly, it seems like The Wizard
may have a far more prominent role than he

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.470
had in the first film.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:28.879
While he primarily served as a mentor figure
and the cause of Billy's powers, the new trailer

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:32.709
makes it seem like the Daughters of Atlas
have a particular ax to grind against the

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:34.050
kindly Wizard.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.310
Early in the trailer, Hespera is seen cursing
Batson and his friends from one side of a

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.249
prison door.

00:02:39.249 --> 00:02:41.801
"Children stole the power of the gods.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:45.412
You ripped it from our father's core."

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:49.650
While we don't see who she's talking to, there's
a high chance that it's The Wizard, who is

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.920
later seen blowing gold dust out of a window
while seemingly trapped in a cell.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.250
Are his past sins coming back to haunt him?

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.130
Will he have enough power to help his champion
win the day?

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:03.050
Maybe not, especially given that his trusty
staff is being passed around like a mystical

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.220
hot potato.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:08.410
We also know from a previous teaser that there
will be some new mythical creatures introduced

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.000
to Billy Batson's world in "Fury of the Gods."

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.060
A herd of black unicorns and a craggy-looking
dragon that breathes blue fire were the two

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.319
types of beasties on display in our first
look at the upcoming movie.

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:21.430
But the film's second trailer adds more creatures
to the mix.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.500
There appears to be a chimera tearing apart
New York City during one of the teaser's most

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.110
heart-stopping moments.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.620
Also briefly visible is a black minotaur-like
figure wreaking havoc in the big city.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.069
While the dragons appear to be under the full
control of Kalypso and Hespera, and the unicorns

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:40.400
seem to have been tamed by Billy and his siblings,
it's anybody's guess how the other mythic

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.140
creatures get involved in the action.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.430
Still, it definitely appears that "Shazam!

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.709
Fury of the Gods" is going to have fun with
the mythological aspect of Billy's roots when

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:50.760
the movie takes off on March 17.

